    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers, and moved every value derived from the customer code onto that new identity.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `util/CustomerCode.java`:\n- `of(owner)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`: REGION via the shared `Locality.of(postcode, city)` derivation (postcode-first, city fallback), HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. It's a pure function of the owner's own fields \u2014 no repository lookup, no sequence.\n- `regionOf(owner)` reads the region segment from an assigned `customerCode`, falling back to `Locality.of(postcode, city)` when no code exists (e.g. legacy seed owners with `NULL` customer_code) \u2014 so no regression there.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 now just `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.of(owner))`; dropped the unused `OwnerRepository` parameter.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 `locality` now derives from the customer-code identity via `CustomerCode.regionOf(owner)` instead of computing region independently.\n\n**Followed automatically** (already read `owner.getCustomerCode()`): the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit, and the create audit line \u2014 all now reflect the region-and-hash code (visible in the audit output, e.g. `customerCode=NSW-F4F6FF62`, `VIC-0C44CCFD`).\n\nThe 8 spec checkpoints (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp17, Cp21, Cp30, Cp31, Cp32) and the full 45-test suite all pass.",
